# API Standards (V1)

## Response Format
All API responses must follow the standard envelope structure.

### Success Response
```json
{
  "success": true,
  "data": { ... }, // Object or Array
  "meta": { ... }  // Optional: pagination, counts
}
```

### Error Response
```json
{
  "success": false,
  "error": {
    "code": "ERROR_CODE",
    "message": "Human readable message",
    "details": [ ... ] // Optional validation errors
  }
}
```

## Implementation

### Using Response Handler
Use the `responseHandler` middleware utility (if available) or standard helper functions to ensure consistency.

```typescript
// ✅ CORRECT
res.json({
  success: true,
  data: result
});

// ❌ INCORRECT
res.json(result);
```

### Error Handling
Throw typed errors or pass to `next(err)` for the centralized error handler to process.

```typescript
// Validation Error
if (!valid) {
  throw new ValidationError('Invalid input');
}

// Not Found
if (!item) {
  throw new NotFoundError('Item not found');
}
```

## Route Structure
- `/api/v1/resource` (List)
- `/api/v1/resource/:id` (Detail)
- Use standard HTTP methods: GET, POST, PUT, DELETE.
